  "type": "Example",
  "number": "1.4.2",
  "title": "Determining if circuit elements deliver or absorb power.",
  "body": " Determining if circuit elements deliver or absorb power   For each circuit element in , determine if it delivers or absorbs power.   A circuit composed of four unknown circuit elements all connected in series.   One circuit element is labeled A and has a voltage of VA measured from top to bottom. The + end of element A is connected to the - end of element B, labeled with a voltage of VB measured from left to right. The current I is depicted as flowing left to right through this element. The - end of element B is connected to the - end of element C, labeled with a voltage of VC measured from top to bottom. The + end of element C is connected to the + end of element D, labeled with a voltage of VD measured from right to left. The - end of element D is connected to the - end of element A.     Current flows from high to low potential in elements B and D: therefore B and D are absorbing power. Current flows from low to high potential in elements A and C: therefore A and C are delivering power.   "
