  "body": " Calculating current from voltage and resistance   Calculate the current through the resistors, as shown in the circuit diagram below.   A circuit used to calculate an unknown current.   Circuit with one mesh. The high potential end of an 8V source connects to one end of a 2k resistor. The other end of the 2k resistor connects to one end of a 3k resistor. The other end of the 3k resistor connects to the low potential end of the 8V source. Current Ix is defined as flowing toward the low potential end of the 8V source.     Calculate the equivalent resistance of the two resistors. The two resistors are both in the same branch and are therefore in series.     The circuit can be re-drawn.   A reduced circuit used to calculate an unknown current.   Circuit with one mesh. The high potential end of an 8V source connects to one end of a 5k resistor. The other end of the 5k resistor connects to the low potential end of the 8V source. Current Ix is defined as flowing toward the low potential end of the 8V source.     The current is flowing from high to low potential, so the sign (direction) of the current will be positive. (If the current had been defined in the other direction, then it would be measured from low to high potential and the sign would be negative.)      "
