  "body": "  Calculate the equivalent resistance (between nodes a and b) of the resistors shown in .   Circuit diagram corresponding to .   Circuit with 10k, 1.8k, 24k, 4.7k, 2k, 5.6k, 18k, and 6.8k resistors and seven nodes. 10k, 1.8k, and 4.7k connect at node b. 1.8k, 2k, and 24k connect at node a. 24k and 5.6k connect at node c. 4.7k and 18k connect at node d. 2k, 18k, and 6.8k connect at node e. 6.8k and 5.6k connect at node f. 10k connects at g.       Use either a delta-wye transform or a wye-delta transform.    20.4 kΩ    There are two sets of series resistors that can be combined. The first set is the 4.7 kΩ and 18 kΩ resistors, with an equivalent series resistance of 22.7 kΩ. The second set is the 6.8 kΩ and 5.6 kΩ resistors, with an equivalent series resistance of 12.4 kΩ. The circuit can be re-drawn.   Circuit re-drawn with series resistances combined.   Circuit with 10k, 1.8k, 24k, 22.7k, 2k, and 12.4k resistors and five nodes. Nodes are labeled same as previous. 10k, 1.8k, and 22.7k connect at node b. 1.8k, 2k, and 24k connect at node a. 24k and 12.4k connect at node c. 2k, 18k, and 12.4k connect at node e. 10k connects at g.     Either a wye-delta transform or a delta-wye transform can be done to reduce the circuit. The following solution utilizes a wye-delta transform. The wye resistances are highlighted in red.   Circuit re-drawn with wye resistances highlighted in red.   Same circuit as previous with 2k, 22.7k, and 12.4k resistors in red.     Calculate each of the delta resistances.     Re-draw the circuit.   Circuit re-drawn after the wye-delta transform.   Circuit with 10k, 1.8k, 24k, 28.36k, 15.49k, and 175.84k resistors and four nodes. Nodes are labeled same as previous. 10k, 1.8k, 28.36k, and 175.84k connect at node b. 1.8k, 24k, 28.36k, and 15.49k connect at node a. 24k, 15.49k, and 175.84k connect at node c. 10k connects at g.     The two resistances (1.8 kΩ and 28.36 kΩ) between nodes a and b are in parallel and can be combined, with a parallel resistance of 1.69 kΩ. The two resistances (24 kΩ and 15.49 kΩ) between nodes a and c are in parallel and can be combined, with a parallel resistance of 9.41 kΩ. The circuit can be re-drawn.   Circuit re-drawn with parallel resistances combined.   Circuit with 10k, 1.69k, 9.41k, and 175.84k resistors and four nodes. Nodes are labeled same as previous. 10k, 1.69k, and 175.84k connect at node b. 1.69k and 9.41k connect at node a. 9.41k and 175.84k connect at node c. 10k connects at g.     The 1.69 kΩ resistance is in series with the 9.41 kΩ resistance. The equivalent resistance is 11.11 kΩ. The circuit can be re-drawn.   Circuit re-drawn with series resistances combined.   Circuit with 10k, 11.11k and 175.84k resistors and three nodes. Nodes are labeled same as previous. 10k, 11.11k, and 175.84k connect at node b. 11.11k and 175.84k connect at node c. 10k connects at g.     The 11.11 kΩ and 175.84 kΩ resistances are in parallel with each other. They have an equivalent resistance of 10.45 kΩ. The circuit can be re-drawn.   Circuit re-drawn with parallel resistances combined.   Circuit with 10k and 10.45k resistors and three nodes. Nodes are labeled same as previous. 10k and 10.45k connect at node b. 10.45k connects at node c. 10k connects at g.     The equivalent resistance is the series combination of the remaining two resistors.     This will not be solved using delta-wye transforms. Do this as a practice exercise. The equivalent resistance calculation should be 20.45 kΩ regardless of the method used to calculate it. As a hint, the following circuit diagrams show the two possible delta configurations that can be used in a delta-wye transform. The delta resistances are highlighted in red.   Circuit highlighting one possible delta configuration.   Circuit with 10k, 1.8k (red), 24k, 22.7k (red), 2k (red), and 12.4k resistors and five nodes. Nodes are labeled same as previous. 10k, 1.8k, and 22.7k connect at node b. 1.8k, 2k, and 24k connect at node a. 24k and 12.4k connect at node c. 2k, 18k, and 12.4k connect at node e. 10k connects at g.      Circuit highlighting another possible delta configuration.   Circuit with 10k, 1.8k, 24k (red), 22.7k, 2k (red), and 12.4k (red) resistors and five nodes. Nodes are labeled same as previous. 10k, 1.8k, and 22.7k connect at node b. 1.8k, 2k, and 24k connect at node a. 24k and 12.4k connect at node c. 2k, 18k, and 12.4k connect at node e. 10k connects at g.      "
