  "title": "",
  "body": "  Calculate in the circuit shown in .   Circuit diagram corresponding to .   A circuit with two meshes and three nodes contains a current source \"Is,\" a voltage source \"Vs,\" an 8k resistor, and a 20k resistor. Is and the two resistors connect at node A. The current source flows out of node A. The 20k resistor and high-potential end of Vs connect at node B. The current source, 8k resistor, and low-potential end of the voltage source connect at node C. The current source flows into node C.       3.125 mA    While this circuit appears complicated, the key is to note that the branch through which is defined contains a known resistance and known voltage drop. This means that all other circuit elements (the current source, voltage source, and 20 kΩ resistor) are irrelevant to calculating .  Use Ohm's law to calculate . Note that is defined as flowing from low to high potential and therefore must have a negative sign.      "
