  "title": "",
  "body": "  Calculate mesh current in the circuit shown in . Assume that each mesh contains at least one linear circuit element.   Circuit diagram corresponding to .   Nine meshes are arranged in a 3x3 pattern. Every mesh current is clockwise. From top to bottom, left to right, the mesh currents are labeled I1, I2, I3, etc. through to I8. The central mesh is labeled \"Ix.\"            Note that all of the numbered mesh currents are also branch currents. The only mesh current that isn't a branch current is in the center ( ). Use the relationship between branch and mesh currents to calculate . Note that is defined in an opposing direction to all adjacent mesh currents, which is why the signs of each numbered mesh current is negative.   "
