  "body": "  Calculate the current through and power consumed by the 2 kΩ load resistor in the circuit shown in . (Express this current as a positive value if it flows from to ground, and negative if it flows from ground to .) Then, calculate the current sourced by the op-amp. (Express this current as a positive value if the op-amp sources the current, and as a negative value if the op-amp sinks the current.)   Circuit diagram corresponding to .   Op-amp circuit with 8V source and 2k resistor. The circuit has 3 nodes. The high-potential end of the 8V source connects to the non-inverting input of the op-amp at node A. The inverting input of the op-amp, output of the op-amp, and 2k resistor connect at node B, labeled Vout. The low-potential end of the 8V source and 2k resistor connect to GND at node C.            The op-amp circuit is a voltage follower. The output voltage is equal to , which is 8 V. Use Ohm's law to calculate the current through the load resistor.     Use to calculate the power consumed by the resistor.     No current enters through the inverting node of the op-amp. Therefore, all of the current that flows through the 2 kΩ load resistor is sourced from the op-amp.   "
