  "body": "  A 50 mH inductor has current as shown in . Derive the piecewise functions for , , and . Assume that current is zero for all time before 0 ms.   Graph corresponding to .   Graph of i(t) in mA plotted with respect to time in ms. The graph is linear from (0,0) to (5,10) then linear to (7.5,0) and then remains zero.            Between 0 ms and 5 ms, the current increases from 0 mA to 10 mA. This represents a slope of   .  The function is therefore equal to during this interval of time.  Use to calculate the voltage during this time interval.     Use to calculate the power consumed by the inductor during this time period.     Between 5 ms and 7.5 ms, the current decreases from 10 mA to 0 mA. This represents a slope of   .  If this function originated at zero, the y-intercept would be 10 mA, representing a function of . However, the function is shifted by 5 ms (or 0.005 s). The function is therefore equal to during this interval of time.  Use to calculate the voltage during this time interval.     Use to calculate the power consumed by the inductor during this time period.      "
