  "url": "ch6-inductors-8.html#ch6-homogeneous-ex2",
  "type": "Exercise",
  "number": "6.6.12",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  Derive equations for and given the circuit shown in . The switch is closed for a very long time before opening at a time of zero seconds.   Circuit diagram corresponding to .   Circuit with 6 nodes consisting of a 5V source, six resistors, one inductor, and an SPST switch. The high-potential end of the 5V source connects to the 200ohm resistor at node a. The 200ohm, 750ohm, and 500ohm resistors connect at node b. The 500ohm resistor connects to one end of the SPST switch at node c. The other end of the SPST switch connects to the 20mH inductor and 30ohm resistor at node d. The 30ohm, 600ohm, and 150ohm resistors connect at node e. The low-potential end of the 5V source, 750ohm, 600ohm, and 150ohm resistors, and 20mH inductor connect at node f. Voltage v(t) drops over the inductor from node d to node f. Branch current i(t) flows through the inductor from node d to node f. The SPST switch is depicted as opening.            Analyze the circuit in the initial steady-state condition. The inductor can be replaced by a short.     Circuit with 5 nodes consisting of a 5V source, six resistors, and a short. The high-potential end of the 5V source connects to the 200ohm resistor at node a. The 200ohm, 750ohm, and 500ohm resistors connect at node b. The 500ohm resistor, 30ohm resistor, and short connect at node c. The 30ohm, 600ohm, and 150ohm resistors connect at node d. The low-potential end of the 5V source, 750ohm, 600ohm, and 150ohm resistors, and the short connect at node e. Voltage v(0) drops over the short from node c to node e. Branch current i(0) flows through the short from node c to node e.     The 30 Ω, 600 Ω, and 150 Ω resistors are shorted by the inductor and can be removed from the circuit.     Circuit with 3 nodes and 2 meshes consisting of a 5V source and three resistors. The high-potential end of the 5V source connects to the 200ohm resistor at node a. The 200ohm, 750ohm, and 500ohm resistors connect at node b. The low-potential end of the 5V source connects to the 750ohm and 500ohm resistors at node c. Branch current i(0) flows through the 500ohm resistor from node b to node c.     Use source transformation to convert the voltage source to a current source.        Circuit with a 0.025A source, 200ohm resistor, 750ohm resistor, and 500ohm resistor. All four circuit elements are connected in parallel between nodes a and b. The current source flows out of node b and into node a. Branch current i(0) flows through the 500ohm resistor from node a to node b.     Calculate the equivalent resistance of the circuit.     Use the current divider rule to calculate .     Analyze the circuit at to calculate the equivalent resistance seen by the inductor.     Circuit with 3 nodes and 2 meshes consisting of an inductor and three resistors. The 20mH inductor and 30ohm resistor connect at node a. The 30ohm, 600ohm, and 150ohm resistors connect at node b. The 20mH inductor connect to the 600ohm and 150ohm resistors at node c. Voltage v(t) drops over the inductor from node a to node c. Branch current i(t) flows through the inductor from node a to node c.     Calculate the equivalent resistance as seen by the inductor.     Use to calculate .     Use to derive an equation for .     Use to derive an equation for .      "
