  "number": "6.6.13",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  Derive equations for and for the circuit shown in . The switch has been open for a very long time before closing at a time of zero seconds.   Circuit diagram corresponding to .   Circuit with 6 nodes consisting of a 120V source, four resistors, inductor, and SPST switch. The high-potential end of the 120V source connects to the 30ohm resistor at node a. The 30ohm resistor, 20ohm resistor, and one end of the SPST switch connect at node b. The 20ohm resistor connects to the 2uH inductor at node c. The 2uH inductor connects to the 40ohm resistor at node d. The other end of the SPST switch connects to the 16ohm and 40ohm resistors at node e. The 16ohm resistor connects to the low-potential end of the 120V source at node f. The SPST switch is depicted as closing.            Analyze the circuit in the initial steady-state condition. The inductor can be replaced by a short.     Circuit with 5 nodes and 1 mesh consisting of a 120V source and four resistors (30ohm, 20ohm, 40ohm, and 16ohm). All circuit elements are wired in series. Branch current i(0) flows through the circuit from the high-potential end of the source to the low-potential end of the source.     Use Ohm's law to calculate .     Analyze the circuit at to calculate the equivalent resistance seen by the inductor.     Circuit with 6 nodes and 2 meshes consisting of a 120V source, four resistors, one inductor, and a short. The high-potential end of the 120V source connects to the 30ohm resistor at node a. The 30ohm resistor, 20ohm resistor, and short connect at node b. The 20ohm resistor connects to the 2uH inductor at node c. The 2uH inductor connects to the 40ohm resistor at node d. The 40ohm resistor, 16ohm resistor, and short connect at node e. The low-potential end of the 120V source connects to the 16ohm resistor at node f. Voltage v(t) drops over the inductor from node c to node d. Branch current i(t) flows through the inductor from node c to node d.     The voltage source, 30 Ω resistor, and 16 Ω resistor are shorted out of the circuit and can be removed.     Circuit with 3 nodes and 1 mesh consisting of a 20ohm resistor, 40ohm resistor, and 2uH inductor. All circuit elements are wired in series.     The equivalent resistance as seen by the inductor is equal to the series combination of both resistors, which is 60 Ω. Use to calculate .     Use to derive an equation for .     Use to derive an equation for .      "
