  "body": "  Derive an equation for based on the circuit shown in . The switch is in position a for a very long time before moving to position b at a time of zero seconds. The component values are , , , , , , and .   Circuit diagram corresponding to .   Circuit with seven nodes consisting of two voltage sources (Vs1 and Vs2), SPDT switch, three resistors (Rs1, Rs2, and R), capacitor C, and inductor L. The high-potential end of Vs1 connects to Rs1 at node c. The low-potential end of Vs2 connects to Rs2 at node d. Rs1 connects to position a of the SPDT switch at node a. Rs2 connects to position b of the SPDT switch at node b. The input of the SPDT switch, R, and C connect at node e. R, C, and L connect at node f. The high-potential end of Vs2, the low-potential end of Vs1, and L connect at node g. Voltage vX(t) drops over C from node e to node f. Branch current i(t) flows through L from node f to node g. The SPDT switch is depicted as switching from position a to position b.            Analyze the circuit in its initial steady-state condition. The capacitor can be replaced by an open and the inductor can be replaced by a short.     Circuit with one mesh and three nodes consisting of a voltage source Vs1 and resistors Rs1 and R. The high-potential end of Vs1 connects to Rs1 at node a. Rs1 and R connect at node b. The low-potential end of Vs1 connects to R at node c. Voltage vX(0) drops over R from node b to node c. Branch current i(0) flows through R from node b to node c.     Use Ohm's law to calculate . This value is continuous with time.     Use the voltage divider rule to calculate . This value is also continuous with time.     Analyze the circuit in its final steady-state configuration to calculate , the value of the particular solution.     Circuit with one mesh and three nodes consisting of a voltage source Vs2 and resistors Rs2 and R. The low-potential end of Vs2 connects to Rs2 at node a. Rs2 and R connect at node b. The high-potential end of Vs2 connects to R at node c. Branch current i(infinity) flows through R from node b to node c.     Use Ohm's law to calculate .     Analyze the circuit at to derive the differential equation.     Circuit with two meshes and four nodes consisting of voltage source Vs2, resistors Rs2 and R, capacitor C, and inductor L. The low-potential end of Vs2 connects to Rs2 at node a. Rs2, R, and C connect at node b. R, L, and C connect at node c. The high-potential end of Vs2 and L connect at node d. Voltage vX(t) drops over C from node b to node c. Branch current i(t) flows through L from node c to node d.     Perform KVL around the entire circuit and solve it for .     Perform KCL at the node connecting , , and .     Plug into and reduce until the differential equation is in standard from.     Plug in numerical values using base units.     Use to calculate the damping parameter and use to calculate the resonant frequency.     This circuit is critically damped. Use to calculate .     Use and to calculate the coefficients of the equation.     Plug everything into to obtain an equation for .      "
