  "body": " Active band-stop filter   A low-pass filter (analyzed in ) and high-pass filter (analyzed in ) can also be used as inputs to a summing amplifier, which leads to an active band-stop filter. This circuit is depicted below.     Circuit consisting of a summing op-amp with two inputs of an op-amp LPF and an op-amp HPF.     The low-pass filter stage sets the lower cutoff frequency of this circuit. The high-pass filter stage sets the higher cutoff frequency of this circuit. The inverting op-amp sets the overall filter gain.   "
