  "title": "",
  "body": "  Derive a transfer function for the circuit shown in . Then, determine the filter type.   Circuit diagram corresponding to .   Circuit consisting of an op-amp, three resistors (R1, R2, and R3), two capacitors (C1 and C2) and voltage source Vin. The high-potential end of Vin connects to R1 at node a. R1, C1, and the non-inverting input of the op-amp connect at node b. R2, R3, and C2 connect to the inverting input of the op-amp at node c. R3, C2, and the output of the op-amp connect at node d. R2, C1, and the low-potential end of Vin connect at node e. Voltage Vout drops from node d to node e.          The circuit is an active, second-order, low-pass filter.    Use the voltage divider rule to calculate the voltage at the non-inverting node, denoted as .     Perform KCL at the inverting node. Everything will be expressed as generic phasor for now.     Reduce the impedance defined in the KCL equation.     Plug the value of into the KCL equation. Reduce to standard form.     Analyze the circuit at . is not zero.     Circuit consisting of an op-amp, three resistors (R1, R2, and R3), and voltage source Vin. The high-potential end of Vin connects to R1 at node a. R1 and the non-inverting input of the op-amp connect at node b. R2 and R3 connect to the inverting input of the op-amp at node c. R3 and the output of the op-amp connect at node d. R2 and the low-potential end of Vin connect at node e. Voltage Vout(0) drops from node d to node e.     Analyze the circuit at . is zero.     Circuit consisting of an op-amp, two resistors (R1 and R2), two shorts (SH1 and SH2) and voltage source Vin. The high-potential end of Vin connects to R1 at node a. R1, SH1, and the non-inverting input of the op-amp connect at node b. R2 and SH2 connect to the inverting input of the op-amp at node c. SH2 and the output of the op-amp connect at node d. R2, SH1, and the low-potential end of Vin connect at node e. Voltage Vout(infinity) drops from node d to node e.     This circuit is an active, second-order, low-pass filter. (Refer to .)   "
