  "body": " Calculating complex power from a circuit diagram   Calculate the complex power consumed by the following circuit. The source voltage is equal to .     Circuit with two meshes and three nodes consisting of voltage source Vac, 2uF capacitor, 120ohm resistor, and 20mH inductor. The high-potential end of Vac, 2uF, and 120ohm connect at node a. The 120ohm and 20mH connect at node b. The low-potential end of Vac connects to the 2uF and 20mH at node c.     First, phasor transform the circuit. The load impedance is equal to the impedance of the capacitor in parallel with the series combination of the resistor and inductor.     Circuit consisting of (17.32-j10 VRMS) voltage source connected in series with (128.37-j56.11 ohm) impedance.     Use Ohm's law to calculate the current through the circuit.     Use to calculate the complex power.      "
