  "body": "  Determine the circuit elements that must be placed on the load (shown as in the circuit diagram) for maximum power transfer given the circuit in . Then, calculate the power consumed by that load. The source frequency is 50 Hz.   Circuit diagram corresponding to .   Circuit with three meshes and four nodes consisting of a (20ARMS angle 45deg) current source, 5ohm resistor, 40mH inductor, 0.5mF capacitor, 8ohm resistor, and unknown Zload. The high-potential end of the current source connects to the 5ohm and 40mH at node a. The 40mH, 0.5mF, and 8ohm connect at node b. The 8ohm and Zload connect at node c. The low-potential end of the current source, 5ohm, 0.5mF, and Zload connect at node d.       The load circuit elements include a 11.2 Ω resistor connected in series with a 32.9 mH inductor.       Phasor transform the circuit.     Circuit with three meshes and four nodes consisting of a (14.1+j14.1 ARMS) current source, 5ohm resistor, j12.6ohm impedance, -j6.37ohm impedance, 8ohm resistor, and unknown Zload. The high-potential end of the current source connects to the 5ohm and j12.6ohm at node a. The j12.6ohm, -j6.37ohm, and 8ohm connect at node b. The 8ohm and Zload connect at node c. The low-potential end of the current source, 5ohm, -j6.37ohm, and Zload connect at node d.     Deactivate the source and calculate the Thévenin equivalent impedance.     Convert the current source to a voltage source.        Circuit with two meshes and five nodes consisting of a (70.7+j70.7 VRMS) voltage source, 5ohm resistor, j12.6ohm impedance, -j6.37ohm impedance, 8ohm resistor, and unknown Zload. The high-potential end of the voltage source connects to the 5ohm at node a. The 5ohm and j12.6ohm connect at node b. The j12.6ohm, -j6.37ohm, and 8ohm connect at node c. The 8ohm and Zload connect at node d. The low-potential end of the current source, 5ohm, -j6.37ohm, and Zload connect at node e.     Use the voltage divider rule to calculate .     For maximum power transfer, the load must be equal to .     Use to calculate the inductance value.     Use to calculate the power transferred to the load.      "
